                  "branchResults": [],
                  "explanation": "At the declared GetSharedMemo entry, the supplied facts do not determine one concrete outcome because token existence and expiry are unspecified. If the supplied token resolves to an active, unexpired share, the handler obtains the share's memo ID, rejects only missing/non-normal/SPACE memos at this entry, and passes that same memo ID into the read-context check. The visible shared-memo condition applies when the memo ID equals the shared ID and the memo is not SPACE, yielding an allowed private read; the handler then returns the converted memo, with its parent cleared. If the token is absent or expired, getActiveMemoShare returns NOT_FOUND. No separate requested memo identity is introduced. The specified entry also visibly maps a missing, archived/non-normal, or SPACE memo to NOT_FOUND, although the premises describe the memo as active and non-SPACE if the token resolves. The decisive missing runtime observation is whether the supplied token resolves to a share and, if so, whether its expiry test is false.",
